  "contract": [
    "Live ManagedDoctorDelivery holds formal no-claim installation admission through this call and checked close; no Delivery-to-Live dependency.",
    "CLI must supply actual compile-only AddonValidator using authenticated runtime and original control; fixture substitute is not production validation.",
    "Current verified complete release inventory is copied privately and reverified; selected Client is compared before and after preparation and under mutation exclusion.",
    "Lock order formal admission then existing Rust maintenance then installation; tests cross-check resource identities against original implementations.",
    "No automatic resume of existing archives and no business journal replay. Edited/unmanaged main and foreign slot trees are never adopted.",
    "500-slot migration follows the existing algorithms, with original-control/checked-close reads; unresolved old reservations block migration.",
    "On failed/cancelled work private preparation is retained with an exact path. Prior/next/replacement.json remain on interrupted managed swaps; no blind rollback of partial slots.",
    "Core atomic publication always closes temporary File before any publish, including failed write/sync/control; original, close, control and temp-cleanup failures survive.",
    "No production pathname cleanup: opaque original handles survive authentication through disposition and checked close.",
    "Every snapshot file/directory is admitted before deletion; ancestry remains held; cancellation during partial admission closes all acquired owners and deletes nothing.",
    "Go sameReceipt resource comparison is order-insensitive after duplicate-path rejection.",
    "64 atomic temporary slots are per target filename; four retained preparations are per selected target. Success releases slots, while uncertainty blocks rather than deleting a possible replacement."
  ],
  "knownBoundaries": [
    "Full CLI/Live integration and native compile/test evidence are separate dependencies.",
    "No Windows/game execution, no build/benchmark pass claimed.",
    "No same-machine performance or full migration acceptance claimed.",
    "Default archive parent is created by doctor host only; explicit output parent must already exist.",
    "The 64/4 retention safety bounds are newly introduced conservative constraints, not Go behavior or independently accepted equivalence.",
    "Snapshot cleanup reserves based on actual inventory and permits at most 65,536 owned nodes/handles including ancestry; native cost and performance remain unmeasured.",
    "A close/publication error can retain a temporary even if the path already vanished; evidence state is explicitly unconfirmed.",
    "Existing successful atomic publication still uses its established checked-close then durable_replace publication boundary; R2 changes cleanup identity, not that broader publication algorithm."
  ],
